          "Young insurgents with rifles and petrol bombs fought Soviet tanks from strongholds such as the Corvin Passage, and on 25 October security forces fired on a crowd in front of Parliament. Workers' councils took over towns across the country. Imre Nagy became prime minister, announced a ceasefire on 28 October, and the Soviets pulled their troops out of Budapest.",
