    "cuban-revolution", "Cuban Revolution", 1953, 1959,
    "Fidel Castro's 26th of July Movement, alongside other opposition groups, waged a guerrilla war against the military dictatorship of Fulgencio Batista. From a small band in the Sierra Maestra mountains the rebels defeated Batista's much larger army in 1958, and Batista fled on 1 January 1959. Castro's new government soon allied with the Soviet Union, making Cuba a Cold War flashpoint.",
